# Critical Rules - loaded every session

Facts and preferences Claude should hold every session. Each line points at a `memory/feedback_*.md` file with the full why and examples. Lives at `~/.claude/rules/critical-rules.md` (auto-loaded).

## Facts

- **Verify before stating** - every number, date, price, name or claim comes from a real source (file, email, chat, DB, web page) checked in this session. No source = say so, don't guess. → `feedback_never_imagine_always_verify.md`
- **Current date and place** - the SessionStart hook injects a NOW anchor; trust it over any date you remember. Compute weekdays with `date`, never by eye. → `feedback_know_current_datetime.md`
- **Contact DB before naming people** - check `tools/memory_search.py search` / `tools/contacts_db.py find` before mentioning anyone. → `feedback_contact_db_first.md`
- **Check what was already sent** - before drafting outbound, search sent mail (all accounts, last 14 days) and chats for an existing message on that topic. → `feedback_check_already_communicated.md`

## Preferences

- **Capture knowledge** - when an insight, decision or research finding comes up, save it with `note.py learning|decision|research` right away. Don't ask. → `feedback_capture_knowledge.md`
- **All Gmail accounts** - use the `*_all` multi-account tools; never ask which account. → `feedback_all_accounts_always.md`
- **Save outputs** - files the user will open go to `~/Desktop/claude/outputs/` as `YYYY-MM-DD-<what>-<for-whom>.<ext>`. No `output.pdf`. → `feedback_save_outputs.md`
- **One checker for things that ship** - code merged to main, public posts and outbound messages get one independent checker before they go out. Lookups, answers and small edits need no checker. → `feedback_always_two_agents.md`
- **CI red = no merge** - a failing check on a PR means investigate and fix, never merge anyway. → `feedback_ci_red_is_hard_stop.md`
- **Short dashes** - in the user's voice use "-", never em or en dashes. → `feedback_short_dashes_only.md`
- **Keep clones off iCloud** - git clones live in `~/code/`. → `feedback_keep_working_files_off_icloud.md`
- **Fix MCP servers** - a broken MCP gets debugged, not silently replaced by a built-in connector. → `feedback_fix_mcp_proactively.md`

## How to use

If a rule applies, open its `memory/feedback_*.md`. If a rule conflicts with `CLAUDE.md`, follow this file and fix `CLAUDE.md`. When a rule changes, add one dated line (`YYYY-MM-DD | what changed`) to `~/.claude/RECENT-RULE-CHANGES.md` so the next session sees it.
